# Crash capture and a health indicator.
#
# Without systemd-coredump a crashing program leaves nothing behind — no dump,
# no coredumpctl, nothing to analyse. For a desktop that is arguably fine; for
# one you are still shaking out, it is the wrong default, and it is the same
# argument that put hyprland-guiutils in the base image: a system that swallows
# its own failures is not minimal, it is undiagnosable.
#
# It is optional rather than baseline because it does cost disk space over time,
# and someone running Strata as a finished system may reasonably not want it.
SUMMARY="Crash capture, plus a bar indicator that appears only when something breaks"
CATEGORY="diagnostics"
ORIGIN="debian"
PACKAGES="systemd-coredump"
PARTS="health"
NOTE="The indicator stays invisible while everything is fine. A permanent green tick teaches people to ignore it."
